    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0536" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.5151/285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-19T15:00:00-05:00">June 19, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. The use of compensation marks by German competitor threatens to deprive
                    American bidders of a contract involving nearly 2 million pesos with the
                    Colombian Government for pipeline for Bogotá waterworks. Full report by air mail
                        today.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d465-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="18" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 83, June 19, 1935, not printed. In despatch No. 194, August 16,
                    1935, the Minister in Colombia reported that the Ministry of Public Works had
                    accepted the bid of American firms (621.6217/23).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
